<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constitution of Guáimaro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1869">1869</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Constitution of Guáimaro was adopted on 10 April 1869 by an assembly of Cuban rebels in the town of Guáimaro, in Camagüey, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a>. It created the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in Arms, with a House of Representatives that elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-manuel-de-cespedes">Carlos Manuel de Céspedes</a> president and held strong powers over him. It also declared all inhabitants of the republic free.</p></div>
